Lobium — native fingerprint config channel + native surfaces (browser reads file → renderer reads base64).

The sidecar writes lobium-fp.json and launches Lobium with --lobium-fp-config=<path>. The renderer is
sandboxed and cannot read files, so — mirroring Chromium's own GaiaConfig file→switch serialization —
the BROWSER process reads the file ONCE (cached; base::ScopedAllowBlocking; kept off the per-spawn hot
path) and forwards its base64 to each renderer as --lobium-fp-data (with a Windows command-line size
guard). The RENDERER's lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() (added module //components/lobium_fp, wired by
core/build-gn.patch) base64-decodes and parses it once and exposes typed fields; every failure path
LOG(ERROR)s (a present-but-unparseable config must never silently leak the host fingerprint).

Native surfaces hooked so far, each reading Current() (all PROVEN on Chromium 152.0.7928.0):
  1. navigator.hardwareConcurrency (navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc) — file value 7 vs host 12,
     consistent main-thread + Workers. --lobium-hwc=<n> retained as a single-value POC fallback.
  2. navigator.deviceMemory + the Device-Memory / Sec-CH-Device-Memory client-hint HTTP headers, hooked
     at their SINGLE shared source ApproximatedDeviceMemory::GetApproximatedDeviceMemory()
     (approximated_device_memory.cc) so the JS getter and the HTTP header report the IDENTICAL value,
     bucket-snapped to a value this build emits (desktop [2,32] / Android [1,8]).
  3. navigator.maxTouchPoints (navigator_events.cc) — 0→5; overrides on the optional's has_value().
  4. WebGL UNMASKED_VENDOR_WEBGL / UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL (webgl_rendering_context_base.cc) — the real
     GPU strings (WEBGL_debug_renderer_info) → cfg->webgl.unmasked_vendor/renderer, overridden as an
     ATOMIC pair (both or neither, so a partial persona can't pair a spoofed vendor with the host
     renderer). One getParameter site covers WebGL1 + WebGL2 (delegation) + Workers/OffscreenCanvas.
     The masked GL_VENDOR/GL_RENDERER stay Chrome's constant "WebKit"/"WebKit WebGL" (real behaviour —
     overriding them would be a tell). This is a genuine native-only surface: a JS getParameter override
     is itself detectable, so CDP cannot do it cleanly.
     KNOWN LIMITATION (deep-surface roadmap, see hooks.md): only the vendor/renderer STRINGS are
     overridden; getSupportedExtensions(), the MAX_* limits, getShaderPrecisionFormat(), the WebGL2
     limit block, and the rendered-pixel hash still reflect the real backend. A detector can cross-check
     the renderer string against those. This is starkest on a SwiftShader dev backend (RTX-3060 string +
     software capabilities); in production the mitigation is (a) never ship SwiftShader as the real
     backend, (b) pin personas to the host GPU class, and (c) incrementally align the extension list /
     key limits / precision + per-profile pixel farbling (seeds.webgl) to the claimed GPU.
  5. Canvas 2D seeded farbling (seeds.canvas) — deterministic ±1-LSB perturbation of R/G/B (alpha
     untouched) on the READBACK surfaces, applied by the shared skia-free kernel lobium::FarbleCanvasRgba
     (//components/lobium_fp/lobium_farble.cc). Keyed on (seed, absolute pixel coord, channel) so it is
     stable-per-profile, distinct-per-seed, differs from the host, and imperceptible. Hooked at FOUR
     readback entries so every path a fingerprinter can read is farbled IDENTICALLY and exactly once:
       (a) getImageData — base_rendering_context_2d.cc, perturbs the private ImageData pixmap in place
           at origin (sx,sy) so a sub-rect read matches the full-canvas read.
       (b) toDataURL — html_canvas_element.cc, via the LobiumFarbleReadback(Snapshot) helper.
       (c) toBlob — html_canvas_element.cc, same helper.
       (d) OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob — offscreen_canvas.cc (a separate encode path; without it a
           worker's convertToBlob would leak the true host hash while getImageData is farbled).
     Farbling is deliberately NOT applied in HTMLCanvasElement::Snapshot(): Snapshot is also the shared
     source-image path (GetSourceImageForCanvas → drawImage / createImageBitmap / WebGL texImage2D), so
     farbling there would perturb ordinary compositing AND double-apply with getImageData. Proven by the
     drawImage regression probe: drawImage(A→B)+getImageData(B) EQUALS direct-draw(D)+getImageData(D)
     (MATCH=true), i.e. drawImage copies unfarbled pixels and getImageData farbles exactly once. All
     hooks are guarded IsRenderingContext2D() so WebGL canvases stay on the WebGL pixel path (coherent
     with gl.readPixels) rather than being made inconsistent by 2D-canvas noise.
     KNOWN LIMITATION (see hooks.md): the noise is position-keyed, so drawing the SAME content at many
     offsets and taking the per-pixel mode could average the ±1 noise away. Real fingerprinters draw
     their probe once at a fixed position, so this is the same theoretical limit Brave's farbling
     accepts; the mitigation (a per-read sub-seed) is deferred as it would break within-session read
     stability, which detectors also check.

platform / UA-CH / languages are NOT hooked here — they are JS-safe/CDP surfaces (MASTER_PLAN §5),
handled by the sidecar's cdp-fingerprint.ts setUserAgentOverride (see hooks.md).

Eight hook points:
  1. content/browser/.../render_process_host_impl.cc — browser reads --lobium-fp-config, forwards base64 --lobium-fp-data.
  2. third_party/blink/common/.../approximated_device_memory.cc — deviceMemory single source (JS + client-hint header).
  3. third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/navigator_events.cc — maxTouchPoints.
  4. third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc — hardwareConcurrency.
  5. third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc — WebGL unmasked vendor/renderer.
  6. third_party/blink/renderer/modules/canvas/canvas2d/base_rendering_context_2d.cc — canvas getImageData farbling.
  7. third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/canvas/html_canvas_element.cc — canvas toDataURL/toBlob farbling (readback helper).
  8. third_party/blink/renderer/core/offscreencanvas/offscreen_canvas.cc — OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob farbling.
